 "title": "Jerusalem, Jerusalem; Lord, Lord; My God, My God",
 "summary": "Three more New Testament passages with doubled words: Jesus laments over 'Jerusalem, Jerusalem' (Matthew 23:37), warns that not everyone who says 'Lord, Lord' will enter the kingdom (Matthew 7:21), and cries out 'Eloi, Eloi, lama sabachthani' — 'My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me?' (Mark 15:34). Doubled words and personal pronouns are colour-coded.",
 "text": [
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Matt.23.37",
   "text": "\"Jerusalem, Jerusalem, who kills the prophets"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Matt.23.37",
   "text": "and stones those who are sent to her!"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Matt.23.37",
   "text": "How often I wanted to gather your children together,"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Matt.23.37",
   "text": "the way a hen gathers her chicks under her wings,"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Matt.23.37",
   "text": "and you were unwilling.—Matthew 23:37"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Matt.7.21",
   "text": "\"Not everyone who says to Me,"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Matt.7.21",
   "text": "'Lord, Lord,' will enter the kingdom of heaven,"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Matt.7.21",
   "text": "but he who does the will of My Father who is in heaven will enter."
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Matt.7.21",
   "text": "—Matthew 7:21"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Mark.15.34",
   "text": "At the ninth hour Jesus cried out with a loud voice,"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Mark.15.34",
   "text": "\"ELOI, ELOI, LAMA SABACHTHANI?\" which is translated,"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Mark.15.34",
   "text": "\"MY GOD, MY GOD, WHY HAVE YOU FORSAKEN ME?\""
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "verse",
   "osis": "Mark.15.34",
   "text": "—Mark 15:34"
  }
 ],
